", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "Accounting and finance are inextricably intertwined. For example, key roles for corporate financial reporting include assisting firms in raising debt and equity capital, improving the efficiency of the capital markets, and facilitating the effective monitoring of corporate managers' investing and financing decisions. This seminar provides a rigorous and integrative exposure to research that addresses economic issues of interest to both the accounting and finance research communities.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GM", "acadGroup": "BU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2713, "crseId": 362108, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "NRE", "catalogNbr": "5110", "titleShort": "PhD Sem. in Emper Corp Finance", "titleLong": "PhD Seminar in Empirical Corporate Finance", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 17861, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "01:25PM", "timeEnd": "04:10PM", "startDt": "08/23/2018", "endDt": "12/04/2018", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "mnc35", "firstName": "Murillo", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Campello"}], "pattern": "F", "facilityDescr": "Sage Graduate Hall 131", "bldgDescr": "Sage Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "SGH131", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Non-Johnson Students ONLY: August 14th at 8:00am thru September 6th at 4:00pm. You may add or drop